WEBVTT

00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:11.375
<i>Fluttering and dancing in the sky</i>

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:17.750
<i>Let our love reach you...</i>

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.500
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.583
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.000
<i>LOVE...</i>

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.042
<i>ohhhh... SAY!</i>

00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:26.458
<i>This heart</i>

00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:28.750
<i>Try and move it</i>

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.875
<i>Look, how should I show you?</i>

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:33.042
<i>Then together with us</i>

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:34.417
<i>Let's dance! Take my hand</i>

00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:35.875
<i>hey yeah yeah!</i>

00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:37.375
<i>Leave it to me</i>

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:40.292
<i>to escort you! ALL RIGHT!</i>

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:43.000
<i>As if worrying, the passing rain</i>

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.458
<i>caressed my cheek gently,</i>
<i>so as not to be noticed.</i>

00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:50.417
<i>Jumping over faster than a shooting star</i>

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.875
<i>Reach out your hand!</i>

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:54.792
<i>let's get LOVE!</i>

00:00:54.792 --> 00:00:56.417
<i>Shout to the moon! (shout!)</i>

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.042
<i>Let your shout ring out! (shout!)</i>

00:00:58.042 --> 00:00:59.208
<i>What's up, what's up?</i>

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:00.958
<i>Let me hear your voice</i>

00:01:00.958 --> 00:01:02.500
<i>Undo your hair</i>

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.500
<i>Saying goodbye to yesterday</i>

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.500
<i>when my eyes were closed</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.042
<i>A single petal fluttering lightly</i>

00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:10.917
<i>Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!)</i>

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:12.750
<i>Shout out your feelings! (shout!)</i>

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>Isn't it fine</i>

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.625
<i>if nothing is for sure?</i>

00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:16.667
<i>wow yeah!</i>

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.167
<i>That's right</i>

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.000
<i>Let's put away the lies</i>

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.708
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:28.625
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:41.792
"On a New Path"

00:01:41.792 --> 00:01:43.417
"On a New Path"
I overslept!

00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.542
Oh, morning!

00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:47.042
Huh? Kai?

00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:48.417
Why are you in the Gravi room?

00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:52.875
Our demon king is visiting, so I'm
making sure he doesn't do anything bad.

00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:53.917
Oh?

00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:56.042
I don't have time for that!
I'm gonna be late for work!

00:01:56.042 --> 00:01:58.083
Oh, wanna bring breakfast with you?

00:01:58.083 --> 00:01:59.458
Kai!

00:01:59.458 --> 00:02:01.417
Koi, how long are you going to eat?

00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:02.917
Coming.

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:04.583
Hurry, Koi!

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:06.583
See you later!

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.542
Okay, have a nice day!

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:13.083
It's really lively this morning.

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:14.458
Oh, morning.

00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:15.875
Morning.

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:18.833
You look sleepy, Hajime.

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:21.042
I'll do something about it by the time I leave.

00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:24.167
Hajime, you're really not
a morning person, are you?

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.958
If you still have time, I'll make coffee.

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:28.500
Thanks, Kai.

00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:33.792
Hello, sleepy king.

00:02:33.792 --> 00:02:38.042
If you were Sleeping Beauty,
I would wake you with a kiss.

00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:39.208
No thanks.

00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:41.708
What are you doing in our common room?

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:47.792
I thought we could take this chance
to watch our dear members together on stage.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:51.917
Oh, the play Aoi and the others are in
is being announced today, right?

00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:52.750
Is it starting?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.375
"The Mysterious Tale of Tsukiuta: Dreamflower"

00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:05.667
This is a question for the lead actors.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:10.333
For this play, you'll be
double leads in your first big roles.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:12.083
What are your thoughts on this?

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:15.458
If I'm gonna do this, I'll make
everyone say I'm the coolest!

00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:17.083
We won't lose to the Gravi guys.

00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:18.167
You...

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.083
I'll give it my all.

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:26.583
You normally work as pop idols, but you
do want to focus more on acting from now on?

00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:29.083
I can't think that far ahead yet,

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:33.000
but I'm looking forward to all
the experience I'll get from this.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.083
Right, Arata?

00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:37.833
Yeah. Please support us in this, too.

00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:42.333
I have a question for your costar, Mr. Mikaduki.

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:49.167
I believe your character this time is one who
supports the young people from the sidelines.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.083
Can you tell us your thoughts on that?

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:56.542
I will focus on my role, just as I always do.

00:03:56.542 --> 00:04:02.542
I don't know about popular idols or anything,
but we have our own rules on the stage.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:05.083
I have no intention of
bending the rules for them.

00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:11.875
As expected of Yuzuru Mikaduki. He's harsh!

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:13.583
Things have gotten interesting!

00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:16.167
--Excuse me!
--Look this way, please!

00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:21.958
We made it through alive, huh?

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:23.792
I was really nervous...

00:04:23.792 --> 00:04:25.542
Huh? Why?

00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:29.250
Mikaduki!

00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:31.458
You're...

00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:34.208
Aoi Satsuki from Six Gravity.

00:04:34.208 --> 00:04:36.583
I'll be learning from you in this play.

00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:39.417
Um, I'm Yoru Nagasaki from Procellarum.

00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:42.083
I'm You Haduki.
I look forward to working with you.

00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:44.250
I look forward to working with you, too.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.125
I'm Arata Uduki. Looking forward to it.

00:04:48.542 --> 00:04:50.250
You're an impudent one.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.750
Sorry! He doesn't mean any harm.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.417
Right?

00:04:55.417 --> 00:04:59.458
I'm Yuzuru Mikaduki.
Sorry about what I said earlier.

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:03.167
If I say something like that,
the press'll make a nice story out of it.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.417
It's all part of being an actor.

00:05:05.417 --> 00:05:07.250
But it was half in earnest.

00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:14.083
I still have doubts about whether you idols
have what it takes to be the leads in a play.

00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:15.958
Don't think badly of me.

00:05:15.958 --> 00:05:17.958
It can't be helped,
since it's a different line of work.

00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:18.625
What?!

00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:19.833
You!

00:05:19.833 --> 00:05:23.167
If you do half-assed work,
I'll work you hard with no mercy.

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:24.583
Later.

00:05:25.917 --> 00:05:27.583
What's up with that guy?!

00:05:27.583 --> 00:05:28.875
He seriously pisses me off!

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:30.333
Calm down, You.

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:34.625
Like I can be calm after someone
so obviously came to pick a fight?!

00:05:34.625 --> 00:05:38.125
Anyway, isn't that spacey guy over there
in more trouble than me?

00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:39.333
Me?

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:40.542
Why?

00:05:40.542 --> 00:05:42.833
He called you impudent, remember?

00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:46.750
Arata's emotions don't really show
on his face, so he's easily misunderstood.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.375
Poor guy...

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:49.792
Don't say that about yourself.

00:05:51.125 --> 00:05:54.500
I'm worried about whether or not You
will be able to get along with Mikaduki.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.917
You heard him, You.
Don't cause trouble for Yoru.

00:05:58.917 --> 00:06:00.583
I know!

00:06:00.583 --> 00:06:03.083
You, too, Arata. Don't cause trouble for Aoi.

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:05.833
You don't need to worry about me.
I wouldn't do that.

00:06:08.583 --> 00:06:10.083
"The Mysterious Tale of Tsukiuta: Dreamflower"
"Rehearsal Space"

00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:14.042
Today, we will have the first rehearsal
for the Uduki-Satsuki pair.

00:06:14.042 --> 00:06:15.583
Look forward to working with you today!

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.583
Looking forward to it!

00:06:17.583 --> 00:06:19.917
Okay, let's start with a read-through.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.125
Wow, we're doing a rehearsal already?
It's just the first day.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.833
Are you nervous?

00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:49.792
Well, since we're doing this,
I want to do a good job acting.

00:06:49.792 --> 00:06:52.250
As expected of the prince.
Always a model student.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.125
Don't call me that.

00:06:55.125 --> 00:06:57.083
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.708
You're the same as usual, huh, Arata?

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:02.042
All I can do is do what I can.

00:07:02.042 --> 00:07:03.917
That's just like you, Arata.

00:07:05.292 --> 00:07:07.125
He's putting his script down already?

00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:08.750
He's amazing!

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:16.458
What is your dream?

00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:18.500
My dream?

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.917
Yeah. You already know
what my dream is, right?

00:07:21.917 --> 00:07:25.458
So now, I want you to tell me your dream, Okita.

00:07:25.458 --> 00:07:28.542
My dream, huh? I...

00:07:28.542 --> 00:07:35.292
Don't you still have things to do before
you talk about dreams, Okita, Nagakura?

00:07:35.292 --> 00:07:36.583
Hijikata, sir...

00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:41.083
Is it wrong to imagine
our dreams, Hijikata, sir?

00:07:41.083 --> 00:07:43.417
I didn't say it was wrong.

00:07:43.417 --> 00:07:45.583
I just meant that it's still too early.

00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:47.167
<i>Still</i>.

00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:52.333
Satsuki, your line!

00:07:52.333 --> 00:07:54.167
Oh, s-sorry!

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:57.000
U-Um... My line...

00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:01.375
Here.

00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:02.875
Thanks.

00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:05.833
Aw man, I feel tired suddenly.

00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:09.500
Yeah. Mikaduki really is amazing, huh?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.708
I see why they call him the best.

00:08:12.708 --> 00:08:13.500
Yeah.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.917
Thanks for that.

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:18.000
Mikaduki...

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.542
Hey, Okita actor.

00:08:19.542 --> 00:08:20.708
Yes?

00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:22.958
You messed up your line earlier, didn't you?

00:08:22.958 --> 00:08:26.667
Even if you're an amateur, if that's what
you're like with the script in your hand,

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.708
you'll have a hard time later.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.625
Arata!

00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:40.417
What are you doin--

00:08:40.417 --> 00:08:43.375
If you have something to say, then say it.

00:08:43.375 --> 00:08:46.833
You've got a long way to go
before you can glare at me, <i>kid</i>.

00:08:49.042 --> 00:08:52.625
Jeez. I was just looking at him.

00:08:52.625 --> 00:08:55.000
I kind of understand how You feels now.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.542
You can't flare up at him like that, though.

00:08:57.542 --> 00:09:01.250
Aoi. Do I look like the type to do that?

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:02.292
No.

00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:04.083
But just in case.

00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:08.000
I don't like that you're being
misunderstood like that.

00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:11.500
Don't worry.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.167
Arata...

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:47.667
You okay, Aoi?

00:09:47.667 --> 00:09:48.792
Yeah...

00:09:48.792 --> 00:09:50.750
I think I might be a little sick...

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.458
We were filming in the rain yesterday.

00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:55.125
Are you okay for rehearsal?

00:09:55.125 --> 00:09:56.625
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:09:57.583 --> 00:10:00.958
It's okay, Arata.
You don't have to worry so much.

00:10:00.958 --> 00:10:04.375
Okay, then. But don't push yourself.

00:10:04.375 --> 00:10:06.333
I won't.

00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:08.625
I swore on this sword

00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:11.708
that I will cut my own path with these hands!

00:10:11.708 --> 00:10:14.375
But, there's no time!

00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:16.125
There's no time!

00:10:16.125 --> 00:10:18.875
You's amazing...

00:10:18.875 --> 00:10:20.167
Stop!

00:10:20.167 --> 00:10:22.333
Good job! You've gotten better!

00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:24.167
Thank you!

00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:27.750
Then next, let's have the
Uduki-Satsuki pair do the same scene.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.125
Yes, sir!

00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:31.333
Mr. Mikaduki, do you need a break?

00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:34.125
I'm fine. Let's continue.

00:10:34.125 --> 00:10:36.458
I swore on this sword

00:10:36.458 --> 00:10:39.167
that I will cut my own path with these hands.

00:10:39.167 --> 00:10:42.625
But, there's no time.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.542
There's no time.

00:10:45.542 --> 00:10:47.000
Stop!

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:51.625
Uduki, you can release your emotions more.

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:53.917
Release my emotions?

00:10:53.917 --> 00:10:57.208
In a play, there's no need to cry real tears.

00:10:57.208 --> 00:11:01.000
But you won't be able
to get your feelings across

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:04.833
unless you go at it with the spirit of
"I'm really going to cry!"

00:11:04.833 --> 00:11:06.208
Yes, sir.

00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:07.083
Sir.

00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:08.583
Hm?

00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:12.208
Can we take a short break after all?

00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:16.708
I'm tired, and it'd be better if
we gave Uduki more time to focus.

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:19.167
Sure. Let's take a ten-minute break!

00:11:19.167 --> 00:11:21.125
No, I can do it.

00:11:21.125 --> 00:11:22.542
I can continue.

00:11:22.542 --> 00:11:23.958
Please let me continue.

00:11:23.958 --> 00:11:25.167
Arata!

00:11:25.167 --> 00:11:26.875
Uduki.

00:11:26.875 --> 00:11:29.458
Nothing will come of you getting worked up.

00:11:29.458 --> 00:11:32.833
You play the main character.
That means you're the leader.

00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:35.125
Take a good look around you.

00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:39.208
Aoi!

00:11:39.208 --> 00:11:40.833
Hey, Aoi!

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:41.750
Mikaduki!

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.417
I'm on break. You rest, too.

00:11:44.417 --> 00:11:46.917
But, I wanted you to understand...

00:11:46.917 --> 00:11:50.833
Arata's emotions don't show on his face,
so he's hard to understand,

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:52.917
but he is serious about doing this.

00:11:52.917 --> 00:11:56.917
His thoughts come out before he thinks,
so he might seem impudent,

00:11:56.917 --> 00:11:57.875
but he's actually--

00:11:57.875 --> 00:12:00.250
That's no good, is it?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:05.167
On stage, there's no point if he can
only communicate to you, his friend.

00:12:05.167 --> 00:12:06.583
If he can't communicate to those around him,

00:12:06.583 --> 00:12:08.583
then he can't move the hearts of the audience.

00:12:08.583 --> 00:12:09.583
Am I mistaken?

00:12:09.583 --> 00:12:14.833
And you... Is this really the time
for you to worry about others?

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:19.167
Stop trying so hard to be a goody two-shoes.
Rest during the break.

00:12:19.167 --> 00:12:23.458
I don't want to stand on the same stage
as a bunch of half-assed actors.

00:12:27.042 --> 00:12:28.458
Arata!

00:12:28.458 --> 00:12:29.583
No, Arata!

00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:31.458
Hey, stop, Arata!

00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:32.875
Sorry!

00:12:32.875 --> 00:12:35.958
Aoi isn't half-assed.

00:12:35.958 --> 00:12:38.583
He's working harder than anyone else.

00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:40.375
Don't just say whatever you want.

00:12:40.375 --> 00:12:41.917
Arata.

00:12:41.917 --> 00:12:42.917
Sto...

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:45.750
Aoi!

00:12:45.958 --> 00:12:47.083
Aoi!

00:13:01.875 --> 00:13:02.958
Aoi.

00:13:02.958 --> 00:13:04.417
Arata...?

00:13:04.417 --> 00:13:06.458
Huh? Where am I...?

00:13:06.458 --> 00:13:08.167
Your room.

00:13:08.167 --> 00:13:10.625
You collapsed at rehearsal.

00:13:10.625 --> 00:13:15.542
Oh no, now I've done it!
We were in the middle of rehearsal, too...

00:13:15.542 --> 00:13:17.833
Yoru stood in for you.

00:13:17.833 --> 00:13:20.542
I see... Sorry.

00:13:22.292 --> 00:13:25.083
You don't need to apologize.

00:13:25.083 --> 00:13:26.500
Arata?

00:13:29.292 --> 00:13:30.750
Sorry

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.083
that I wasn't the first one
to notice you were suffering.

00:13:35.625 --> 00:13:37.583
You don't have to apologize.

00:13:38.583 --> 00:13:42.125
It's my fault for not taking care of myself.

00:13:42.125 --> 00:13:45.042
There was a bunch of stuff I didn't get around
to doing after we started rehearsals.

00:13:45.042 --> 00:13:47.375
It's true that I wasn't doing everything properly.

00:13:47.375 --> 00:13:50.125
That's not true. You--

00:13:50.125 --> 00:13:52.167
You know, I was flustered.

00:13:53.542 --> 00:13:58.542
It was my first time in a lead role,
so I was so anxious and worried,

00:13:58.542 --> 00:14:04.000
but you were the same as usual,
so I thought you were amazing.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.583
Aoi, you're giving me too much credit.

00:14:07.583 --> 00:14:11.208
I was flustered, too. I mean, I still am.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:18.125
No matter how much I read the script,
I can't say things the way I want to.

00:14:18.125 --> 00:14:25.083
Every day, I think about how
I'm not cut out for acting.

00:14:25.083 --> 00:14:26.750
Really?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:31.000
Even so, we have no choice but to do it

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.208
because we were chosen.

00:14:33.208 --> 00:14:35.208
"We were chosen"...

00:14:35.208 --> 00:14:40.917
Yeah. There are a ton of people
who want to be in our position.

00:14:40.917 --> 00:14:45.125
I'm sure there are people more suited
to be lead actors than me.

00:14:45.125 --> 00:14:51.292
But they chose me... <i>us</i>...

00:14:51.292 --> 00:14:56.000
That's why I just have to make up
for what I don't have with hard work.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:57.583
You know?

00:14:57.583 --> 00:15:01.208
Look, it's not like I'm having
an easy time of it, either.

00:15:03.875 --> 00:15:05.458
I guess.

00:15:05.458 --> 00:15:08.500
I see. I think I feel a little better.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.917
You really worry about
stuff like that too much.

00:15:11.917 --> 00:15:13.833
That's just how I am.

00:15:15.083 --> 00:15:16.833
Thanks, Arata.

00:15:21.208 --> 00:15:22.167
Arata?

00:15:22.167 --> 00:15:24.250
How's Aoi doing?

00:15:29.042 --> 00:15:32.708
Oh, good! I was worried after you fell like that.

00:15:32.708 --> 00:15:34.208
Sorry, Yoru.

00:15:34.208 --> 00:15:37.083
Mr. Tsukishiro said he would have them
let you take a break from rehearsals

00:15:37.083 --> 00:15:39.458
until your cold was completely better.

00:15:39.458 --> 00:15:42.917
I'll stand in for you until then,
so rest as much as you need to.

00:15:42.917 --> 00:15:46.708
Thanks. But I feel a lot better already.

00:15:46.708 --> 00:15:49.417
Anyway, it's your fault, Arata.

00:15:49.417 --> 00:15:50.208
Huh?

00:15:50.208 --> 00:15:53.375
Getting angry like that after
I told you not to worry Aoi.

00:15:53.375 --> 00:15:55.375
That made me really nervous, too.

00:15:55.375 --> 00:15:57.875
Well, it's not like I don't
understand how you feel, though.

00:15:57.875 --> 00:16:03.042
It doesn't make me feel good to hear
Yoru or Aoi talked about like that.

00:16:03.042 --> 00:16:04.917
Stop that, You.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:10.958
But Mikaduki says harsh things,
but he might actually be kind.

00:16:10.958 --> 00:16:12.708
What?

00:16:12.708 --> 00:16:15.375
I overheard the staff talking.

00:16:15.375 --> 00:16:18.458
They were saying that he probably
asked for a break suddenly

00:16:18.458 --> 00:16:21.625
because he noticed that
Aoi wasn't feeling well.

00:16:22.792 --> 00:16:27.917
And when I was standing in for Aoi,
he gave me advice.

00:16:27.917 --> 00:16:32.542
He told me how I should act taking into
consideration the quirks in Arata's acting.

00:16:33.833 --> 00:16:37.625
Mikaduki has been the lead
in a lot of different plays,

00:16:37.625 --> 00:16:41.875
so I think he can see things
that we don't notice.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:45.125
I can't beat him.

00:16:45.125 --> 00:16:48.083
Huh? You're only realizing that now?

00:16:48.083 --> 00:16:49.083
What?

00:16:49.083 --> 00:16:51.292
I mean, I move too much in
the sword fighting scenes,

00:16:51.292 --> 00:16:55.292
so he always has to make up
for me missing my marks.

00:16:55.292 --> 00:16:57.750
Afterward, he lectures me a lot, though.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.375
Even though you're good at
remembering dance steps, huh, You?

00:17:00.375 --> 00:17:03.417
Right? It's so frustrating!

00:17:03.417 --> 00:17:07.000
I still get scolded about how
I don't support enough.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.250
It's different from singing, so it's hard.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.000
I'm told not to shout, though.

00:17:15.042 --> 00:17:16.833
Aoi?

00:17:16.833 --> 00:17:19.125
Everyone was the same, huh?

00:17:19.125 --> 00:17:22.292
Not able to do things well, and getting
frustrated and worrying about it.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.625
Yeah.

00:17:25.625 --> 00:17:27.667
Why are you two smiling?

00:17:27.667 --> 00:17:28.875
Did something happen?

00:17:28.875 --> 00:17:29.792
Nope.

00:17:29.792 --> 00:17:31.000
Let's work hard, okay?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.333
So Mikaduki will recognize our ability,

00:17:33.333 --> 00:17:38.042
and so we can make the people
who come see the play happy!

00:17:38.042 --> 00:17:39.042
Yeah!

00:17:45.917 --> 00:17:47.417
Good morning!

00:17:47.417 --> 00:17:49.500
I apologize for causing trouble yesterday.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.750
Are you over your cold?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.167
Yes, it's completely gone.

00:17:53.167 --> 00:17:55.375
Your guard dog isn't with you?

00:17:55.375 --> 00:18:00.083
Oh, Arata is at a different job this morning.

00:18:00.083 --> 00:18:01.083
Oh?

00:18:02.083 --> 00:18:05.458
Um, sorry about Arata, too.

00:18:05.458 --> 00:18:11.917
It might seem like Arata and I were
being defensive, but that's not it...

00:18:11.917 --> 00:18:17.417
Arata got angry at you because I was unreliable.

00:18:17.417 --> 00:18:19.875
I apologize.

00:18:19.875 --> 00:18:25.917
Arata takes you and the play seriously, so--

00:18:25.917 --> 00:18:27.125
Arata!

00:18:35.083 --> 00:18:37.958
I deeply apologize for yesterday.

00:18:37.958 --> 00:18:41.167
I was inexperienced as a lead actor.

00:18:41.167 --> 00:18:43.458
I mean, I still am.

00:18:43.458 --> 00:18:47.292
But I will change. Because I don't
want my friends to worry about me.

00:18:48.542 --> 00:18:54.208
I will show you acting that will make you
think that idols can act pretty well, too.

00:18:54.208 --> 00:18:56.958
Please guide me as you will!

00:19:05.917 --> 00:19:07.875
Let me tell you something good.

00:19:10.542 --> 00:19:13.792
I don't dislike impudent guys.

00:19:13.792 --> 00:19:14.833
Huh?

00:19:53.125 --> 00:19:56.167
"The Mysterious Tale of Tsukiuta: Dreamflower"
"Opening Day"

00:19:56.167 --> 00:19:59.667
"To Aoi & Arata, from your fans"
"Congratulations, from Tsukino Talent Production"

00:19:59.667 --> 00:20:02.417
"The Mysterious Tale of Tsukiuta: Dreamflower"
"Today's Actors"

00:20:02.417 --> 00:20:06.417
"Soji Okita: Arata Uduki"
"Shinpachi Nagakura: Aoi Satsuki"

00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:10.083
Arata, I'm going to the bathroom.

00:20:10.083 --> 00:20:12.833
Calm down, Aoi. You just went, didn't you?

00:20:12.833 --> 00:20:15.750
Huh? O-Oh, right...

00:20:17.167 --> 00:20:18.417
You're too nervous.

00:20:18.417 --> 00:20:19.417
"Strawberry Au Lait"

00:20:20.417 --> 00:20:22.625
Arata, that's not a straw!

00:20:23.958 --> 00:20:27.667
Looks like you're pretty nervous, too, huh?

00:20:27.667 --> 00:20:29.208
Y-Yeah, looks like it.

00:20:30.458 --> 00:20:31.375
Yo!

00:20:31.375 --> 00:20:32.625
Sorry to intrude!

00:20:32.625 --> 00:20:33.250
You!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.333
Yoru!

00:20:34.333 --> 00:20:35.542
What's the matter?

00:20:35.542 --> 00:20:37.167
We just came to encourage you.

00:20:37.167 --> 00:20:39.000
Don't tell me you guys are gonna watch?

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.375
Is that bad?

00:20:40.375 --> 00:20:43.417
No, it's just that you've already
watched us so much in rehearsal,

00:20:43.417 --> 00:20:47.292
so I didn't think you needed to go out of your way
to watch a play that you're gonna be in, too.

00:20:47.292 --> 00:20:49.958
You're not cute at all, are you?

00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:51.917
We'll watch since we have the chance.

00:20:51.917 --> 00:20:55.958
We'll be cheering you on from the audience,
so do your best, Aoi, Arata.

00:20:55.958 --> 00:20:58.500
Surprise that Mikaduki, okay?

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.708
Okay!

00:20:59.708 --> 00:21:01.125
Yeah.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:08.708
Thank you for coming to today's performance of
<i>The Mysterious Tale of Tsukiuta: Dreamflower</i>.

00:21:08.708 --> 00:21:11.000
The play will begin shortly.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.125
For guests still in the lobby,
please take your seats.

00:21:22.875 --> 00:21:26.125
I'm looking forward to this, you two.

00:21:26.125 --> 00:21:28.417
Let's go. The curtain's going up.

00:21:28.417 --> 00:21:29.667
Yes, sir!

00:21:41.958 --> 00:21:47.333
<i>Until our futures make</i>

00:21:47.333 --> 00:21:52.750
<i>large flowers bloom one by one</i>

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:53.750
<i>Hey</i>

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:06.458
<i>You're smiling with an innocent look on your face</i>

00:22:06.458 --> 00:22:11.875
<i>I'll smile in the same way next to you</i>

00:22:11.875 --> 00:22:17.333
<i>I pray that we can stay like this</i>

00:22:17.333 --> 00:22:22.500
<i>forever and ever</i>

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:33.208
<i>But I know that nothing stays the same forever</i>

00:22:33.208 --> 00:22:41.708
<i>Warbler, sing again as the seasons change</i>

00:22:41.708 --> 00:22:45.083
<i>Look for spring</i>

00:22:45.083 --> 00:22:50.875
<i>Precious things become memories</i>

00:22:50.875 --> 00:22:55.708
<i>Even if they spill out of these hands</i>

00:22:55.708 --> 00:22:58.917
<i>We will not stop</i>

00:22:58.917 --> 00:23:07.417
<i>The warmth that is in this chest</i>

00:23:07.417 --> 00:23:09.583
<i>I know what it is</i>

00:23:09.583 --> 00:23:10.833
<i>Right?</i>

00:23:11.917 --> 00:23:14.042
"Episode 5: A Chance Encounter with the Past"

00:23:14.042 --> 00:23:15.583
"Episode 5: A Chance Encounter with the Past"
I'm Kai Fuduki!

00:23:15.583 --> 00:23:18.917
"Episode 5: A Chance Encounter with the Past"
Summer means haunted houses!

00:23:18.917 --> 00:23:20.125
"Episode 5: A Chance Encounter with the Past"
I'm at one for a TV show

00:23:20.125 --> 00:23:22.375
"Episode 5: A Chance Encounter with the Past"
with some of the Procella members,

00:23:22.375 --> 00:23:25.250
but this place seems to
have an interesting history...

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:28.875
Huh? Nothing will happen, right?

00:23:28.875 --> 00:23:32.458
Next time, "A Chance Encounter with the Past."

00:23:32.458 --> 00:23:34.292
Memories of summer.

00:23:34.292 --> 00:23:42.059
Tender, fleeting memories of childhood.
